WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.292
Ten PDF tips that save me time every week.

2
00:00:05.792 --> 00:00:11.890
Page ranges, smart compression, signing, OCR and the order I run things

3
00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:15.755
in. Small habits that make PDF work painless.

4
00:00:17.155 --> 00:00:20.270
1. Learn the page range syntax.

5
00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:26.904
Almost every PDF tool in OpenFile accepts ranges like 1-3, 7, 10-.

6
00:00:28.204 --> 00:00:31.597
4. Scans are images, treat them that way.

7
00:00:31.597 --> 00:00:35.073
A scanned PDF is mostly pictures of pages.

8
00:00:36.373 --> 00:00:41.875
7. Redact properly. Drawing a black box over text in most viewers does not

9
00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:43.883
remove the text underneath.

10
00:00:45.183 --> 00:00:49.945
10. Chain it in the Workspace. If you do the same steps every week, the

11
00:00:49.945 --> 00:00:53.567
Workspace can run them as one recipe on a whole batch.

12
00:00:54.867 --> 00:00:57.871
To try it, open Merge PDF in OpenFile.

13
00:00:57.871 --> 00:01:02.376
Drop in a file, adjust the settings and press the button.

14
00:01:02.376 --> 00:01:06.408
It all runs on your device, so nothing is uploaded.

15
00:01:08.108 --> 00:01:12.396
Read the full post, with live demos, on the OpenFile blog.
